From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 02:04:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 45/51] coh 77: untimed hot paths in build-70 shape; probe
 calibration
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Instrumentation only (no protocol change):
- KV Get: the untimed Get is the artifact's Get plus exact counts; timed Gets
  run GetTimed (out of line). ReadFromCXL, read_seq_start/end and
  write_seq_start/end are build 70's bodies plus one dispatch branch to their
  timed variants; GetAnchor is build 70's body (GetAnchorTimed separate).
- read_seqlock_begin: the contended spin out of line (fast path = upstream).
- NR: combine_until_synced costs only upstream's loop test when synced; timed
  anchors receive a pointer for the dispatch cycles (no thread-local access
  or call next to the dispatch); the anchor flag is set by the C++ caller.
- Timed variants are deliberately not marked cold: a cold placement made a
  timed section cost ~1.5 us and would bias the sampled durations.
- Probe calibration at Register: median of back-to-back TSC pairs ->
  ThreadAnchor.reserved[1] (ns), [2] (ps); timed-event counts (A), (B)+(C),
  (D) -> reserved[3..5] for the subtraction rule (rackobj.h, M2 §19).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
